{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund","id":1580,"title":"Compact: SG-14; The Bund","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-03T00:36:48-07:00","id":1580,"title":"Compact: SG-14; The Bund","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Schutzgruppe 14<br /> \u201cThe Bund\u201d</b></span></div> <br /> Germany doesn\u2019t like to talk about World War II. It was a nation\u2019s darkest moment, the time when German culture was subverted by madmen and human monsters. After the war the Allied nations that saw the end result of Hitler\u2019s \u201cFinal Solution\u201d forced the Germans to see the horrors their inaction had unleashed, forcing entire communities to walk through the death camps and ghettos to see exactly what happened when a person gave up their morals for safety and prosperity.<br /> <br /> Put simply, it worked. West Germany learned to internalize that kind of hatred of what it had done, while the East merely tried to please its Soviet masters. West Germany embraced its roots before Hitler, rebuilding itself as an industrial nation on par with what it had been before World War I. A new constitution was written to remind both Germany, and indirectly the world, that human rights were not violable. That people of all kinds were to be accepted and protected. The German military powerhouse before 1945 was made subservient to the government again and the German states made self-governing while the Federal government of Germany oversaw the affairs of the nation on the world\u2019s scale. When Germany became one again, a hole had been filled.<br /> <br /> So when the Allies also found the fullest extent of what Hitler\u2019s SS and Gestapo had been doing during the war, from trafficking in relics to consorting with witches, they at first tried to utterly destroy Germany\u2019s occult secrets. Some organizations stripped Germany of its occult assets, others did their best to expatriate those \u201clesser\u201d Nazis whose knowledge could be used for a positive purpose. Small cells of soldiers and occupying forces seeing the horrors that lurked behind mankind on the battlefields and in the ruined cities went about clearing the monsters from the German states, but soon realized that perhaps they had been too hasty in their attempt to destroy what could possibly be used to protect Germany once they had left. So, in the utmost positions of power, the generals and politicians of America, Britain and France had to enact a way to protect Germany from its occult crimes.<br /> <br /> Their solution was the Bundesamt f\u00fcr Verfassungsschutz, the Federal Office for the Protection of the Constitution. A rough equivalent to the United States FBI formed initially on crushing neo-Nazi and communistic elements in West Germany, the Allied-backed compact was inserted in a small line item in the BfV's second budget. With a shortage of \u201cqualified\u201d hunters, the Allies were forced to accept former Gestapo agents into the ranks of Schutzgruppe, men who had not only hunted the seditious elements under the orders of the swastika but also combated vampires and rogue witches in running street battles even against their \u201callies\u201d in the SS and Wermacht that had decided to throw in their lot with the monsters.<br /> <br /> This is the story of Schutzgruppe 14.<br /> <br /> Their first missions were primarily in support to other organizations from the Allies; assisting TFV in scouring German rocket bases for advanced technology guarded by paranormal threats, or giving MI18 vital information on potential Nazi sympathizers high in government that had been part of the Reich\u2019s .<br /> <br /> To the comfort of many other monster hunting groups, the Gestapo contacts in the BfV were soon revealed after the first president of the BfV defected to East Germany, and reforms were instituted through Schutzgruppe. It was decided that the compact needed to be divided, to prevent the forces inside from gaining \u201cseditious ideas\u201d against the government. SG-14 has since then focused on the elimination of Germany\u2019s paranormal threats.<br /> <br /> Typically, SG-14 recruits its agents not through the military or German police departments, but through universities and colleges. The chief of SG-14 wants agents who are intelligent and able to improvise to new situations, not ones who are willing to break out the firepower at the slightest haunting. Agents are evaluated not only on their ability to handle the paranormal, but also on their willingness to question their superiors\u2019 orders if the situation seems suspicious. They are given training with firearms, but they also have training to a specialty they are assigned, or based on possible prior experiences in the Vigil.<br /> <br /> <i>[Image: A young woman, blond hair in a tight bun, holding an H&amp;K MP7 and a cross. She is wearing a uniform of the Bundespolizei and has an iron cross on her left breast. She is firing at something to her right but her face is merely scowling.]</i><br /> <br /> <b>For the Fatherland?</b> <div align=\"center\"><b>No.</b></div> <div align=\"right\"><b>For humanity.</b></div> <br /> <b>The Divide</b><br /> <br /> SG-14 was split due to the fear that Germany\u2019s leadership would once again decide they would attempt to form a new German empire. Initially split into four primary sections, named \u201cJaghunds\u201d, each section is expected to be expertly trained and knowledgeable in their chosen specialty, whether that be witches for \u201cBlau Jaghund\u201d or the incorporeal for \u201cSchwarz Jaghund\u201d. In theory this plan was meant to both streamline operations on certain monsters and help prevent collusion to usurp the government should its initial ex-Gestapo agents decide they wanted to return to Hitler\u2019s Reich.<br /> <br /> In practice, there are growing issues with the system. In an age where governmental organizations are becoming more and more interconnected, using redundant systems to prevent dramatic failures in intelligence gathering and action, SG-14 steadfastly refuses outright to enact such reforms. Partly out of tradition, but partly out of (some would say outdated) fear of what might happen should they merge.<br /> <br /> There is also a small but present gap between the conventional government and SG-14\u2019s operations. While it appears that other groups utilized by other governments combat monsters under an almost glaring level of anonymity, SG-14 must work its way through the BfV in order to secure its funding and continue its operations. While the president of BfV knows that SG-14 exists and continually gets reports on its operations, details never go beyond that which can be explained through mundane words. Secrecy is kept only because the truth would never make it past the first secretary.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the Bund keeps excellent track of its hunters not only operationally, but psychologically as well. At least three trained psychiatrists are on hand at BfV headquarters for members of SG-14, and members can elect for voluntary leave should they need it. Though it can at times result in manpower shortages, SG-14 considers a stable agent more valuable than a strung out scarecrow.<br /> <br /> <b>The Enemy</b><br /> <br /> There are seven acknowledged Jaghunds in SG-14, but only four existed at their founding. Three more were added over time, and rumors continue to fly that there is an eighth Jaghund, which the leadership promptly shoots down. Each Jaghund focuses on a specific \u201cthreat entity\u201d, each with a single database that flows into one single database accessible only by command itself. Generally, SG-14 tries it\u2019s best to observe and determine if a monster, if not friendly, can at least be counted as non-hostile like a residual haunting or a sentient flock of birds who only want a place to roost. If the monster is proven as a threat to the civilian population, the specific Jaghund will commence offensive operations.<br /> <br /> So do other hunter groups count as an enemy? Without a doubt. SG-14 has formed over the years a large database of disparate groups through Germany, from radical cells of workers in Berlin to Catholic operations in Bavaria. Mostly, these operations keep tabs on these other groups and making sure that, while they cannot fully control their actions, SG-14 can at least keep their actions under some umbrella of organizational control.<br /> <br /> Yet there is one group that the Bund will attack without pause. A group of occultists calling themselves the Loyalists of Thule, remnants of the Thule-Gesellschaft, the occult force that allowed Hitler\u2019s Aryan ideals to lead to the death of millions. Any trace of this society is found, interrogated, and shipped off to blacksite prisons where they serve out the rest of their lives atoning for their atonement.<br /> <br /> There are other groups too. The Vril Society still lives, lurking in the understrata of Germany\u2019s cities, while larger conspiracies attempt to subvert Germany into their fold. The near collapse of the Eurozone is weighing on SG-14\u2019s budget, and the BfV\u2019s accountants are starting to ask questions.<br /> <br /> Yet of anything else, the biggest target that SG-14 goes after are neo-Nazis and other white supremacists. They will sabotage any rally they can, murdering certain demagogues in the night. They consider it being the sin-eaters of Germany, swallowing the filth of their nation so that the innocent can sleep peacefully at night again.<br /> <br /> In times of desperation, the members of SG-14 can be seconded to the Bundespolizei and Landespolizei, in the cases of large-scale urban unrest and national emergency. Yet even then, SG-14 agents are ordered to observe for any paranormal activity, to ensure that even if the crowd gets rowdy, people can walk away alive.<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes</b><br /> <br /> Loyalists of Thule: Tinkering with such evils is what drove Germany into the darkest depths mankind could dive to. If they want to atone, they\u2019ll do it by our rules.<br /> <br /> Null Mysteriis: We attempt to contract them, exchange our money for their knowledge, but they consistently turn us down on \u201cideological grounds\u201d. What do they fear by exchanging their knowledge with us?<br /> <br /> Task Force: VALKYRIE: The Americans still think they are the world\u2019s policeman, and it\u2019s not entirely inaccurate to say they have started to lie down on the job. But they helped to save the world when we attempted to destroy it, and now they are allies. Treat them as such.<br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru: The bunker had to be redesigned again, the bastards nearly breached the door this time. It\u2019s time they realized that we will not allow these evils to see the world as long as we guard them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T00:45:12-07:00","id":1582,"title":"","content":"<b>Hunters</b><br /> Your graduate degree in literature was on the topic of Germanic folklore in the modern age, specifically the belief in fairies as written by certain neo-pagan groups. Then one of those groups approached you, drugged you, and nearly had you sacrificed to a real fairy. That was when the undercover SG-14 member started shooting and broke up the ceremony, offering you a job. You\u2019re researching the same things now, only it\u2019s telling fact from fiction.<br /> <br /> You were a member of the <i>Heer</i>, stationed in Afghanistan, working alongside Americans and British as you tried to bring order to a land that seemed to actively fight it. That\u2019s when you started seeing the ghosts of your dead allies as you were on patrol. Trying to shake it off, you were discharged and took the first plane home, and the ghosts followed you. That was when and SG-14 agent who could also see ghosts came to you and offered to help you get your friends\u2019 spirits to move on. Two weeks later, your wounds have healed, and your friend in SG-14 has your seat all ready for you. First assignment? Save a family from their relative\u2019s ghost.<br /> <br /> The Black Forest nearly killed you when the giant wolf came after you. Your fianc\u00e9 died fighting it, but he bought you enough time to get to the car and onto the road, only to break down barely a mile from the thing. You wandered for days, looking for help while avoiding the monster, when a hiking party of college students walked up on you. You tried to run to them for help when the students brought out guns and shot the monster dead. Impressed at your survival skills, you\u2019ll be nominated for SG-14 when you\u2019re out of counseling.<br /> <br /> The river you lived on had fish-men in it, you knew for sure it did. They came out every month to exact a price for the peace in your village. You wanted to fight them, but the village was almost under a spell. So you had to take action. On the night they went to the center of the town, you covered the banks of the river in pitch and waited. When they started marching back, you ploughed through them in your car, until none were left alive, and then burned the bodies. The Stadspoliezi wanted to string you up for nearly burning your village down, but then two men from the BfV came in to your defense. You listen to the doctors, so why do you still want to find more fish-men to kill?<br /> <br /> Your shame is that your grandfather was a member of the SS. It\u2019s been drilled into you every day since secondary school that your family would never, should never forget that he served at the Death\u2019s Head. So one night you went to Dachau alone, intent on burning the place down so that your family might finally live in peace. That was when you ran into a man shouting about Thule, and getting ready to use the camp as his offering to get there. You didn\u2019t hesitate to pour the gasoline on him and fire the flare gun. As he burned, a helicopter got you in the spotlight. For killing a known enemy of Germany, and for not burning his supply of occult information, you were offered a post in SG-14. You finally found a way to break the chain in your family\u2019s history.<br /> <br /> <b>SIDEBAR: WEISS JAGHUND<br /> <br /> The conventional line of thought goes that if enough people say something is real, there\u2019s a good chance it is. Well more than enough agents agree there\u2019s an unofficial \u201cWhite Hound\u201d that is tasked with the absolute worse missions, and filled with the worst hunters to carry out the missions assigned. There are differences to each story, however, and four have become the norm.<br /> <br /> 1) It\u2019s the Loyalists or the Vril Society, no one\u2019s quite sure which. The important thing is they\u2019re trying to weasel in through SG-14 to the files Kennel has, files that no one else should ever be meant to see.<br /> <br /> 2) They\u2019re a deeply embedded black op trying to find Germany a means to put them on an even footing not only with the monsters, but the more powerful hunter organizations. They\u2019re known to abduct monsters and bring them back for \u201ctesting\u201d.<br /> <br /> 3) It\u2019s a body harvesting op by one of the bigger players in the Vigil. Cheiron is a likely culprit, though TFV or Section 9 wouldn\u2019t mind a few subjects either. Whatever conspiracy it is, they plan on using the information to eventually burn the Bund from the inside.<br /> <br /> 4) There is no \u201cWhite Hound\u201d. The whole thing is just that, a rumor, and anyone claiming to be from it is a liar and a threat. After all, hunters are like sailors and actors, and suspicion and fear are a part of the experience. So what do humans do when they\u2019re afraid? They make stories to rationalize their fear.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T00:54:02-07:00","id":1584,"title":"","content":"<b>HUNDEH\u00dcTTE /THE KENNEL</b><br /> <br /> The command cell for the Bund, Hundeh\u00fctte observes the actions of SG-14 through Germany, ensuring that all operational cells act in line with their specific specialty. It also coordinates requests (Or more accurately, lack of requests) by the leaders of Jaghunds for specialists from other Jaghunds to advise or assist on other cases, or to act on information in cases from opposing Jaghunds.<br /> <br /> The Kennel is located within the HQ for the BfV, in a far back office section that houses a small library of files on previous cases and information. Despite being only made up of a single cell, each member of the Kennel is an expert at administration and public administration, ensuring that cells in the field never have to fear for their supplies. Conversely, this means that few agents in Kennel have any field experience. Despite this, agents of the Kennel don\u2019t long for glory. They come in, do their jobs, and live to continue to do so. Each file is accounted for, and each weapon is tracked, with the famous German efficiency and diligence.<br /> <br /> Despite their efforts, the Kennel is still a governmental office. Files are still misplaced or misnamed, the agents in the field might not give enough details to the agent on the other end of the phone, and sometimes a simple sick day can mean that a phone call asking for orders goes unanswered.<br /> <br /> The enemies of the Kennel aren\u2019t monsters, they\u2019re the bureaucrats trying to make a name for themselves by trying to cut wasteful spending. Often, these are easily deflected by the greater BfV, but with the Eurozone struggling to keep afloat, more of these bureaucrats are showing up calling for an audit on SG-14. The fear is that the enemies of Germany who hide in the shadows can use these means to subvert Germany\u2019s protection, so each member of the Kennel is briefed on how to wrangle the budget and keep things quiet. This means each member of the Kennel learns quickly how to navigate the national bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b> To gain status in the Kennel, an agent just does their job, nothing else matters, measured by how successful they are at being a go-between for agents in the field. However, if an agent is blatantly fouling up the tasks given to them then status is easily dropped.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 1:</b> You\u2019re given the brunt of the office work; filing junk reports, cross-referencing previous incidents, and occasionally squashing a small flying spider with a thick binder. Mercifully, you also get the specialty: Government Files for either Research or Investigation, as well as the Bureaucratic Navigator merit automatically.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 3:</b> After a couple of years, you\u2019ve started to gain a knack for making sure the agents that contact you get their equipment quickly and with exactly what they\u2019d need by getting the proper forms filled. Treat this as Politics: Paperwork.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 5:</b> You know the insides of the file room inside and out, and you\u2019ve been out in the field at least once on observation, and seen what the field agents go through. You can apply this as a version of the Encyclopedic Knowledge merit, but only in regards to the files and information stored by Schutzgruppen 14.<br /> <br /> <b>SILBER JAGHUND/SILVER HOUND<br /> Therianthropes</b><br /> <br /> Silver Hound was the first of the original four jaghunds formed to combat the paranormal in post-WWII Germany. Werewolves roamed nearly unchecked after the Nazis fell from power, stealing and murdering through Germany, the situation only exasperated by the now-proven nonexistant \u201cWerwolf\u201d partisan movement that the Allied forces had to investigate. From 1950 onward, Silber Jaghund hunted through Germany\u2019s cities for werewolf packs that had decided it was easier to kidnap, rape and kill than live as productive members of society, with its remit eventually expanding to include all shapeshifters in Germany\u2019s borders.<br /> <br /> Typically, Silver Hound tries to understand werewolves, reminding themselves that persecution of an entire group for the crimes of the few can lead to darker places. So Silver Hound attempts to communicate with wolf tribes and packs, letting them know that they are not to be killed simply for existing. Understandably, most werewolves simply try to run and hide, or fight the agents sent to find them. It was only after an incident involving GSG-9, a farm in Lower Saxony, and a blood-soaked barn, that SG-14 found a wolf-blooded human willing to talk.<br /> <br /> As far as can be determined, there are two factions of werewolves; one that attempts to patrol the world destroying spirits that would threaten humanity, and a faction that wants to force humans to the positions of breeding stock and worse. Other shapeshifters usually try to stay away from the larger conflicts of the world, and Silver looks over them on a case-by-case basis. If the shifter is merely a deer-woman trying to find a place where she and her flock can roam and graze in peace, the government will advise them on places safe to stay. If the shifter is a cat-man stalking the ghettos killing criminals that escape the law, that\u2019s when Silver breaks out the weaponry.<br /> <br /> Despite their name, Silver has discovered that the silver bullet might be worthless against a shapeshifter. If the creature isn't a werewolf, a trial an error process has to be undertaken to find a specific chemical weakness of some kind in case of future conflicts against a similar breed. It's resulted in many casualties over the years, and the fact is that these files are few and far between. Most agents have to put in some time to actually find anything useful.<br /> <br /> Frequently, Blue unit is attached to Silver\u2019s operations, since many witches have the ability to morph into animals with their own powers. Red sometimes is attached as well, since some vampires have the powers to become wolves or swarms of bats. Usually, Silver agents don\u2019t give a damn. They just file the paperwork and shunt the agents back to their own hounds as soon as the mission is completed.<br /> <br /> More often, an agent of Black unit causes the most problems for Silver. Since some spirits can cause bodily \u201cadaptations\u201d in a human being, but lack any vulnerability to metals, many a Black Hound liaison has been killed or wounded trying to expose the target to a spirit\u2019s ban instead of a therianthrope\u2019s weakness. While Silver understands what the Black liaisons are there for, they still would prefer it if Black learned to slow down their spirit search until the target is restrained securely to make sure if it\u2019s a therianthrope or actual spirit-possession.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b> To gain status in Silver Hound, members need to ensure either the safe negotiation on behalf of Germany to shapeshifters, thus avoiding conflict, or conduct research on shapeshifters that reveals unknown data on the creatures. Murdering a shapeshifter, while valuable, is not seen as highly as the previous two.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 1:</b> The predatory aura that surrounds many shapeshifters stops affecting you as heavily. When affected by Lunacy, treat your Willpower as 1 higher than it is.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 3:</b> You\u2019ve learned a lot about various breeds of shapeshifters. Apply this as an Occult specialty to a specific type of shapeshifter.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 5:</b> You\u2019re at the point where you\u2019re able to practically smell the shapeshifters, no matter what they look like. Treat this as the Unseen Sense merit applied specifically to a single species of shapeshifter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 12-08-2013, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T00:57:14-07:00","id":1585,"title":"","content":"<b>BLAU JAGHUND/ BLUE HOUND<br /> Witches, Psychics, Relics</b><br /> <br /> Witches were heavily embedded into the Nazi regime during the war, and when the Reich fell, these witches scattered. Some attempted to cling to the power they had gained during the war, others tried to quietly extend their lives for a time when the glory of the Aryan race could live again. Other witches worked tirelessly to destroy Nazism, seeking a way to end the horrors their beliefs were put through, whether they were gypsies who practiced folk healing or psychics who tried to battle in secret with their abilities.<br /> <br /> Blau unit was formed alongside Rot unit, to track down witches that collaborated with the Nazis to find new occult weapons and systems to ensure an Aryan victory. Himmler himself was a major proponent of the occult, and when he committed suicide, many of his secrets went to the grave with him. So Blue was forced to search through camp after camp, lab after lab, holding the threat of trial over many members of the research staff who had gone into hiding for information.<br /> <br /> One group escaped this purge; a group of perfect hermaphrodites, with a single eye on back of their skull behind their hair, known as the Eisler Group. This group, guilty of assisting in experimentation on political and religious prisoners, is reportedly still in existence, with its surviving members still alive despite their age. Despite scattering to the winds, Blau has evidence that indicates some of these individuals are still in Germany, practicing their dark arts.<br /> <br /> In the case of other witches, Blau tries to approach them in their civilian lives, trying to work with them in understanding what they do with their powers, how these powers function, and which witches are which. A hausfrau casting little spells of hearth and home harms no one, while a cult built around arcane power and human sacrifice usually gets multiple cells to destroy it. Psychics are approached similarly; an old man using his abilities to find killers for the police is different from a horny teen using his \u201cgifts\u201d to force women into his bed.<br /> <br /> Relics are a different matter. Records indicated that the Nazi government found many in both the deserts of Africa and the snowy wastes of Scandinavia. Whether these really won the war in the early years for Germany, or were so dangerous that they were sealed away, Blau Jaghund is tasked with finding the hiding places for these relics. So far, nothing concrete, and it doesn\u2019t help that some groups would kill to find these powerful artifacts. Other relics are cataloged, filed, and kept in secure facilities to ensure that they cannot be used by others.<br /> <br /> More often than not, Blau must grudgingly work alongside Silber in cases of recorded shapeshifting, often because the shapeshifter might be nothing more than an unfortunate victim that, hopefully, can be turned back. They also need to go in alongside many Rot kill-teams, since what might be a vampire is possibly a witch using blood-based sorcery.<br /> <br /> Where Blau runs into the biggest problems, however, is in trying to work alongside Agency Cooperation. Blau has information on groups such as the \u201cCult of the Phoenix\u201d, the \u201cGuardians of the Labyrinth\u201d, and other occult groups inside of Germany\u2019s borders that are most definitely using magic or magic-empowered objects. The Kennel and AZ usually let a single attach\u00e9 from Blue accompany an AZ team on missions, but for now, command is content to let these hunters do the dirty work for the Bund until they start causing trouble, something that worries Blue Hound.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b> Witches are often still human beings, and need to be treated as such. Successfully finding and negotiating with a witch to ensure their abilities are only utilized in times of either extreme need or at the government\u2019s behest earns a healthy amount of respect from an agent\u2019s superiors. Killing a witch without evidence they were even dangerous, however, can mean a massive drop in status.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 1:</b> You don\u2019t know everything, but you know enough of the basics about witches. You gain the specialty Occult: Witchcraft<br /> <br /> <b>Status 3:</b> As time goes on, you\u2019ve become skilled in certain specific subsets of occult practices and their followers. You get the following two specialties for free under Occult: Alchemy, Cultural Beliefs, Paganism, Satanism or Superstitions.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 5:</b> You\u2019re an expert at waiting out the wizards and witches now, knowing exactly when they\u2019re using their abilities that will prove what they are. All Perception rolls are considered Rote Actions, the equivalent of the Trained Observer merit in Dogs of War.<br /> <br /> <b>ROT JAGHUND/RED HOUND<br /> Vampires, Ghouls</b><br /> <br /> Red has a relatively straightforward mission compared to many of the other jaghunds; find vampires and their blood slaves. The trick then becomes finding where the vampires are hiding, and how to get to them. Vampires have never been a major problem in Germany, but it has been known by Rot Jaghund that vampires moving from Eastern Europe attempt to settle in Germany, in hopes of avoiding old ties. Native vampires sometimes adopt the trappings of Nazism, in order to give themselves an air of mystery and diabolical natures.<br /> <br /> To effectively fight these beasts, Rot has to enter into their world. Agents are sent in undercover, given fake IDs and backgrounds as bloodslaves or ghouls. Certain agents become the willing servants of the vampires, others feign resistance as they are slowly brought into the vampire\u2019s web of servants and slaves. They are monitored as best as they can be by fellow agents, and try to keep their minds clear as vampire blood and powers suck their minds into black pits that allow for only a microscopic chance of escape. Countered with the threat of non-governmental hunter groups looking to kill off as many slaves as they can, or worse, save them without proper understanding of what they\u2019re getting themselves into, and Rot unit has no stroll in the park.<br /> <br /> Rot unit works slow. It drains back accounts, it dismantles ghoul societies. If a lower ghoul becomes suspicious, the Rot operative is authorized to neutralize their threat. If a vampire from an opposing faction is attempting to overtake another, Rot operatives will try to coordinate efforts to destabilize both. Yet Rot Jaghund can\u2019t be everywhere, and at times a single vampire without a large power base can simply be staked and sent into the sun with little issue. And the ghouls left behind after the vampire is ash? The budget is strained enough; rehabilitation is the ghoul\u2019s own problem.<br /> <br /> Often, Rot is made up of those who have already had negative encounters with vampires already, becoming driven in their hatred of the creatures that ruined their lives once before, primarily undercover agents. For the rest of the Jaghund, the members are trained in staking and killing any vampire they come across, and getting undercover Rot agents out of danger. While many other hunters see this as more mercy than most vampires deserve, the rest of SG-14 does not think much of Rot Jaghund. Rot has filed multiple reports that vampires already have a society that polices itself, and information from both &quot;friendly&quot; (bribed) vampires and other hunters seems to indicate that if Rot somehow managed to destroy all of vampire society in Germany, this would leave any survivors alone, and desperate to do whatever they needed to in order to survive. Not only that, but Hundhutte feels that Rot is often far to quick to judge.that all vampires are worth a stake. In an organization that prides itself on being willing to look into the realities of the hidden world, the fact that many Rot operatives have suffered from negative actions at the hands of vampires makes Rot a possible point of contention within the organization.<br /> <br /> Since vampires have such a varied number of supernatural abilities, and their ghouls can take on such abilities as well, Red and Blue Hounds have often started fighting each other over keeping a valuable ghoul informant alive, and often times Blue unit reports fail to mention the blood-magic being used by the \u201cwitch\u201d that died from rapid aging.<br /> <br /> Silver also never gives Red much rest. From vampires turning into wolves, bats, and even a sentient horde of insects and bugs, Red often has to remind a Silver attach\u00e9 that the target isn\u2019t going to fall, no matter how much silver they pump into it. Silver bullets have already been tried against vampires; the squad that tried is still unaccounted for.<br /> <br /> An attach\u00e9 is also usually put into Gelb Jaghund, in order to ensure that the undead being hunted is truly undead and not a vampire, something the Rot attach\u00e9 will almost always go out of their way to prove.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b> In Rot unit, status is easily gained by gathering as much information as possible on vampiric societies and targets. Elimination of an undead enemy garners some recognition in the Bund, but not much.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 1:</b> You don\u2019t know much about vampires in the field, but you\u2019ve read plenty of Rot Jaghund\u2019s files to make up for it. Gain the Occult: Vampire specialty for free.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 3:</b> You\u2019ve seen plenty of the tricks up a vampire\u2019s sleeve, and even though you aren\u2019t immune from them, you\u2019re as ready as you\u2019ll ever be. Take either two dots in the Indomitable merit, or the Unbondable merit, the only time this merit can be taken outside of character creation. All other prerequisites apply as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 5:</b> Having killed enough bloodsuckers and their slaves, you\u2019ve learned to read the signs of when they\u2019re around. Treat this as Unseen Sense: Vampires, or if your ST chooses, Unseen Sense: Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 12-08-2013, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T01:04:27-07:00","id":1588,"title":"","content":"<b>SCHWARZ JAGHUND/ BLACK HOUND<br /> Ghosts, Spirits, Demons, Incorporeals, Possession</b><br /> <br /> Schwarz cut its teeth on some of the world\u2019s worst hauntings, hauntings so strong and spiritual scars so deep, many in the unit know that their jobs will never be finished. They have gone to Dachau on seven separate occasions to keep the spirits inside from spilling out. Bergen-Belsen has only just recently been deemed fully safe for tourist visits. Buchenwald always has one possession a week, and a member of the Jewish faith trained in exorcisms is kept on retainer at all times. They\u2019re just about given up on clearing Auschwitz, and Treblinka hasn\u2019t even gotten a dent in it, so they\u2019ve set up checkpoints to ensure those leaving are clean.<br /> <br /> The ghosts Schwarz fights are not only the ghosts and spirits of the dead. They are fighting the ghosts of a dead ideology that wanted to overwhelm the world with its hate. With that hate, thousands of ghosts and spirits were formed, looking to return Germany to its Third Reich, combined with the hundreds of ghosts and spirits that appear on German soil every day, from Teutonic knights claiming medieval castles to spirits of the Black Forest looking for hosts to spread the wild lands to where it used to be.<br /> <br /> Of all the jaghunds, Schwarz agents are the most likely to be or become more spiritual in their actions, thought spiritual or religious convictions are not necessary for the position. Yet the constant interaction between the dead and demonic beings that exist can force Schwarz agents to accept that sometimes a spiritual explanation is sometimes right, and reconcile their own beliefs on such matters.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re also the most likely to travel and liaise with other groups outside of Germany. Due to the nature of possession and spirit hosts, an agent may have to hunt down a tourist who went back home with more than a few souvenirs, or find a traveling group of German nationals who are carrying an anchor object, if not being anchors themselves.<br /> <br /> Often, Black Hound sends an attach\u00e9 to \u201cwork\u201d with Silver. They\u2019ve noticed there is an upswing in spiritual activity near wolf dens, and do their best to try and accompany any Silver cell with a specialist ready to exorcise the spirits possessing the humans nearby. Silver just tries to ignore the attach\u00e9 until the subject can be subdued.<br /> <br /> Blue and Black Hounds also don\u2019t get along easily when it comes to spirit-focused investigations. Some witches are able to channel the abilities of spirits to their will, primarily for more criminal activities. Blue always feels the witch is the bigger problem (that which possibly little more than a living anchor), but Black wants to go the safer route and remove the witch\u2019s serving entities. Which is why Blue always tries to make a run for the goal and eliminate the possible witch, and why Black has to prove that only the spirits need neutralization.<br /> <br /> Rot and Schwarz rarely interact except where rampant vampiric activity is the cause of a recent upswing in an area\u2019s spiritual activity. Often the two simply deal with their separate problems and try to not step on each other\u2019s toes.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b> Status is gained in Black Hound by either resolving the unfinished business of a ghost or spirit, as well as exorcising demons. Gaining information on various types of incorporeal creatures or just destroying a ghost\u2019s anchors are also valuable. To lose status is incredibly difficult, but should an agent simply focus on the target and not the human cost around them, other agents may find their reports suddenly cited as a red light by the Kennel.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 1:</b> Schwarz might not have all the knowledge they need, but they have enough to give their agents an upper hand. Treat this as Occult: Ghosts.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 3:</b> Schwarz has a supply of secret, supposedly blessed items (WOD Rulebook pg 214) that have detrimental effects on ghosts, spirits and demons. Blau knows nothing about them since Schwarz agents take care to exclude them by calling them \u201cdestroyed\u201d in the records. The Kennel knows the truth, but for now lets the actions continue. The Spezialgebiet Ausr\u00fcstung collection continues to grow.<br /> <br /> In mechanical terms, this means all three-dot and higher members of Schwarz Hunde gain a two-dot blessed object or, Storyteller permitting, a two-dot relic related to ghosts/spiritual/demonic activity. This can be created using either the endowment equation for the Aegis Kai Doru or rules from Reliquary.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 5:</b> Despite all logic on how it might work, your name is known around the invisible world, and it\u2019s not exactly well received. Every spirit you come into contact with instinctively flees in your presence. This can either be the Null merit (Spirit Slayers pg 140), or the Saintly merit (Book of Spirits pg 110).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>GR\u00dcN JAGUNHUND/GREEN HOUND<br /> Interdimensional Entities, Alternate Dimensions</b><br /> <br /> Green Hound formed in the wake of the neopagan revival of Germanic beliefs in the 1980s. Fearful this was an attempt to utilize paranormal forces to recreate a German empire, the Kennel formed a mixed group of agents to discern exactly what was happening. Made up primarily of Schwarz and Blau agents, with two agents from Rot and Silber, Gr\u00fcn tracked some of the neopagans to a ritual where animals were being handed over to something that had horns growing from its forehead and a beard of thick holly bushes. Breaking up the gathering and taking prisoners, the resulting interrogations led to the creation of Gr\u00fcn Jaghund in 1987.<br /> <br /> Green has had to dive deep into German and Scandinavian folklore for more detailed information. Members typically keep a hand-forged iron combat knife on them at all times, even off-duty. Some trawl through abduction support groups for stories that don\u2019t appear to be the result of drugs or drinking, while others scan the missing persons through the nation for cases that lack a clear explanation, if any at all for the disappearance.<br /> <br /> Green has actually made some small headway into reaching out to the native changeling community in Germany, offering them refuge in exchange for information. Sometimes these changelings are more trouble than they\u2019re worth, and Gr\u00fcn is constantly trying to prevent its own agents from being stolen back into the strange dimension the fae call home. Other instances have Green running to and fro as mediators, trying to prevent the creatures from killing each other, and innocent people in the process. These are rare incidents, however, as most changelings are often willing to throw an agent to the dogs to protect themselves from being taken again.<br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly, this causes no end of moral problems for Green. The changeling creatures were, at one point, human, and are similar to the thousands of refugees and foreign nationals that reside in Germany for asylum. Treating changelings as a group as criminals and unwanted individuals strikes too close to the past for comfort, yet trying to root through their social structure, freeholds, and whatever they classify themselves into takes time that could have been spent trying to prevent these issues in the first place.<br /> <br /> A more pressing weakness is manpower. Green is a relatively new part of the Bund, and so is understaffed compared to the other Hounds. As more and more fairies are discovered Green has more and more reason to recruit other hunters into their unit. Right now, barely anyone has answered. Most human beings that have had interactions with fae are either hopelessly enslaved, maddeningly obsessed, or drugged to the gills. To recruit from these pools makes them, and by extension the rest of the Bund dangerously compromised. Yet as more dreams are turned to nightmares and citizens turned into something utterly alien, Green is going to have to make a choice soon.<br /> <br /> Green has also been tasked with the exploration of other dimensionalities, where it runs into the most friction with others Hounds. Black and Green have been locking horns for years now, Black trying to prevent Green from prying into their investigations. Green is convinced that ghosts are part of another class of breaches in the dimensional fabric, and need to be compared to fairies.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b> Green is more interested in finding fae gatherings than individuals. Locating a changeling market or just a house full of the creatures will make it easier the next time Green agents must go fairy hunting. Loss of status can occur if a fae creature is eliminated without proper reasons as to why. Too many dead changelings, and AZ might come calling.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 1:</b> All new agents are given a cold iron combat weapon, the same material that is said to have a detrimental effect on fae. The agent gains not only a specialty in said weapon, but that weapon deals either 2 lethal or 3 bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 3:</b> Learning in the field has taught you more than using the Gr\u00fcn handbook. Treat this as a 9-again on Occult rolls related to fae or the Hedge, as well as other dimensions.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 5:</b> After dozens of experiences with dimensional breaches and fae slave rings, you\u2019ve nearly gained a sixth-sense to finding them. You gain Unseen Sense: Fairies, though seeing through the mask that hides them is another matter entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 12-08-2013, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T01:08:10-07:00","id":1589,"title":"","content":"<b>GELB JAGHUND/YELLOW HOUND<br /> Reanimates, Undead, Misc</b><br /> <br /> Everyone knows that Victor Frankenstein created his horror in Germany, not far from Ingolstadt in Bavaria. Few know that the Nazis made copies of this research, in the hopes of creating a race of expendable super-soldiers to use as shields for more valuable living troops. From the bodies of Soviet prisoners, the minds of American and British prisoners, and the \u201cmiscellaneous\u201d parts of various others, the Nazi SS though they would be able to create the perfect soldier in little under a year.<br /> <br /> Come the 21st century, and Gelb unit is still trying to rectify what had happened. After only a few weeks of the project, the German military burned the base it was on and evacuated the area, leaving whatever prisoners were left to their fate and the monsters they created to hopefully rot. Gelb wasn\u2019t so lucky. Some of the creatures being tested on escaped into Germany, and into the wider world during the post-war confusion. Some followed the course the Monster took in the book, fleeing towards the Arctic Circle. Others followed fleeing Nazis to South America, hiding out in the slums and rainforests. Since the rediscovery of such monsters during the L\u00fcneburg Heath Fire in 1975, Yellow has had to follow each lead through the decades, tracking each monster with only half-burned SS records to guide them.<br /> <br /> Yellow has a reputation for being one of the most emotionless of the various Hounds. Where other agents will at least try to relax and take their minds away from the horrors they have seen, Yellow agents appear introverted and separated from the rest of mankind. The unit has one of the highest washout rates in SG-14, and the average expectancy for green members is roughly three months, taking into account the relative rarity of intelligent reanimates and the strange emotional magic that surrounds them.<br /> <br /> More commonly, the emotional toll comes from whenever Yellow agents are called to neutralize an infestation of zombies and other unintelligent undead. The detachment is a necessary evil, so the agents don\u2019t dwell on the people that they have to eliminate in the course of their actions. Cases of Yellow agents putting bullets through their heads after neutralizing a \u201cfamily\u201d of zombies are unnervingly common, and the Kennel has one dedicated psychiatrist in Yellow\u2019s offices at all times, and another constantly travelling to check on the various field agents.<br /> <br /> A smaller unit than the others, Yellow is out of its depths when it comes to proper cataloging and identification of its targets. Intelligent reanimates are rare creatures, and the unintelligent undead have so many varying causes that marking them all down takes time. It also gets the brunt of the Bund\u2019s stranger cases, from cryptid sightings in the Black Forest to UFO reports on the Baltic. In reality, it\u2019s the dumping ground for cases that the other jaghunds have no real interest in pursuing without the necessary push from the Kennel. This also forces the few hunters in Gelb to become experts at dealing with the unexpected, able to deal with what at first appears to be a spaceship, only for a long tentacle to form out of its landing legs.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b> Since no one really cares about the undead the way they worry about vampires, Yellow operatives can easily gain status by killing any reanimated or undead they come across. Any even better indicator of status is successfully cataloging a new entity or incident for the Bund\u2019s files.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 1:</b> Since they deal with them the most, green Yellow agents learn as much as possible about the strange or the undead. This translates as either an Occult specialty in either Forteana or Undead.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 3:</b> With all the weird shit you\u2019ve seen, Yellow agents often find comfort in the thing they use most; their weapons. They gain the Favored Weapon merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 5:</b> By this point, most Yellow agents have either washed out or are so hardened they barely feel anymore. They also know exactly what\u2019s out there now. This acts as either Unseen Sense: Divine Fire (the life source of some reanimated monsters), or Unseen Sense: Forteana.<br /> <br /> <b>AGENTUR ZUSAMMENARBEIT/ AGENCY COOPERATION<br /> Slashers, Hunters, \u201cInternal Matters\u201d</b><br /> <br /> Despite the rather benign name, the various Hounds quake when they hear it. The Kennel only keeps them in reserve, for times when the crisis is truly great. The reason for this fear? AZ watches the watchmen.<br /> <br /> \u201cPublicly\u201d implemented after a disastrous incident involving a rogue member of SG-14 (rumored to still be on the run today in the Ardennes), AZ\u2019s duty is to police not only SG-14, but all of Germany\u2019s hunters to prevent civilian casualties and knowledge of the paranormal. This remit affords them not only great respect, but a large amount of fear from their fellows. With one recommendation, an AZ agent can not only have a fellow hunter imprisoned, but darker rumors suggest that AZ agents are allowed to \u201cterminate on sight\u201d, a rare order even for the emotionless members of Yellow Hound.<br /> <br /> At first, AZ was a rumored \u201cfifth\u201d hound in the earliest days that the Bund was formed, comprised of Allied personnel ordered to make sure that the earliest Gestapo elements in SG-14 were kept in line. As time passed and the Nazi elements were removed, AZ was expanded to investigate cases of the \u201cM\u00f6rder\u201d, or \u201cSlayer\u201d phenomena. Eventually, it was also tasked with investigating the newly reunited Loyalists of Thule after the farmhouse bombing outside of Paris in \u201968, which gradually involved investigating other hunter organizations within Germany\u2019s borders.<br /> <br /> AZ has had to deal with everything, from amateur filmmakers trying to expose monsters to the world, to Catholic terrorists attempting the firebombing of government offices to \u201cexpose the corruption\u201d. It also has the daunting task of combing through the BfV files to cross-reference any serial murder cases with possible slayer sightings.<br /> <br /> This also means that, in the course of its duties, AZ has had to imprison and even kill its fellow Bund hunters. The Kennel only hands down such orders when the evidence is clear and present, but the fact that they cannot let the members of the target\u2019s Hound know what is ordered means that AZ hunters are seen as little more than cold blooded killers, blindly following orders without questioning the morality, earning them the enmity and fear of all other SG-14 agents.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b> Despite what the other Hounds think, agents in AZ gain status for proving at their fellows aren\u2019t going insane or are plants for other groups. It can also be gained by either convincing smaller hunter groups to put down their torches and give up the Vigil, or recruiting more experienced hunters into SG-14.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 1:</b> In order to prove their fellows are still loyal, AZ hunters need to be skilled in finding out everything about another hunter. This becomes a specialty in only one of the following: Investigation: Body Language, Larceny: Electronic Security, or Streetwise: Body Language.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 3:</b> You\u2019ve formed a web of informants across a wide spectrum of hunters and specialists in the paranormal. This becomes two dots in the Contacts merit, as long as it applies to hunters or hunter groups.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 5:</b> The field is not a place for you anymore, but you can still pour over the data you get from the safety of your computer. You also have a younger AZ agent as a free two-dot Retainer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:06:56-08:00","id":16379,"title":"","content":"Brilliant. Absolutely brilliant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T02:23:43-08:00","id":16532,"title":"","content":"I actually think this is pretty tasteless and don't really understand the niche it fills in Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T18:44:40-08:00","id":16894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=16532#post16532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think this is pretty tasteless and don't really understand the niche it fills in Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about it was tasteless? Did I accidentally write something insulting? Or is it just bland?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T20:06:29-08:00","id":16905,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think if you're going to imply a supernatural cause for something like the holocaust it has to be a lot better than this. What I see trivialises. It also seems to be written from (and probably informed by) a very American perspective, lacks focus and I wonder what anybody would want to use it for beyond 'I want to be in an organisation that has a ton of toys and maybe redeem Germany for the events of the Second World War I guess'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:42:59-08:00","id":16992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=16905#post16905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think if you're going to imply a supernatural cause for something like the holocaust</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund#post1580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Germany doesn\u2019t like to talk about World War II. It was a nation\u2019s darkest moment, the time when German culture was subverted by madmen and <b>human monsters</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to criticize something, at least read it first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T05:17:51-08:00","id":17081,"title":"","content":"I'm talking about subtext and references found in places like the stereotypes tab, Kings Raven. I know you're more of a literalist, but you really have to think harder than that when you're using topics like this. The very premise that killing monsters is somehow going to redeem/prevent holocausts is what trivialises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T05:50:19-08:00","id":17093,"title":"","content":"If you're going to make an accusation like that you have to do better than some nebulous subtext. You know, actually justify why you think so. I certainly don't see anything saying that they believe in killing monsters to redeem themselves (that's the loyalists) or that killing monsters will somehow prevent another holocaust. Rather they have an over-goal, protecting the German government from being co-opted by anything. That includes preventing modern all-too-human neo-nazi's from acquiring influence (something the real life German police are very proactive about) but also taking down vampires (who as Requium will show, are keen on coopting governments).<br /> <br /> BTW Flyboy. Which jaghund is it that deals with neo-nazi's and cults in general?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T06:05:56-08:00","id":17097,"title":"","content":"I haven't made 'an accusation', I've simply said that this does not treat something horrendous respectfully and I have already justified why I think so. Subtext isn't 'nebulous' it's a very basic part of writing, one which you seem determined to ignore for the sake of the power fantasy while chomping at the bit to be a content creator. It really is on the writer to justify their use of things as repellent and resonant and ingrained in the popular consciousness as this. And the human aspect -- the political, the economic, the historical -- seems like an afterthought at best. I think the very foundation of this conspiracy is not up to par. I invite the author to justify it/share why they have decided Hunter needs this conspiracy, and I don't think your defensive tone helps anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T06:17:39-08:00","id":17099,"title":"","content":"Calling a concept insensitive to the holocaust is an accusation by definition, and I never said subtext was nebulous. I said your pointing at subtext was nebulous, because you didn't give any explenation as to why that subtext suggested what you claimed it did.<br /> <br /> And no, it is not on the writer to justify using the Nazi's; I think the history of media, from Dads Army to The Atrocity Archives shows that it's perfectly acceptable to use the Nazis in a story. I haven't seen the writers justifying why the Loyalists of Thule should exist either, or justifying why the Daksha should have dark ties to Nazism. If you think it's done badly enough to criticise, the burden of proof is on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T06:26:12-08:00","id":17103,"title":"","content":"For the record I also dislike the Loyalists of Thule. I'm unfamiliar with everything you've cited as 'perfectly acceptable nazi use', but one appears to be a sitcom and the other is called 'atrocity archives', so I doubt you're speaking from a position of great empathy here. I've explained my position on this and why I've come to the conclusions I have. That the author is beyond reproach, blameless by default, and citing precedent in an old British sitcom seems like a very childish position to take, although it does go a ways to explaining a lot of your custom content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T06:41:05-08:00","id":17105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=17103#post17103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so I doubt you're speaking from a position of great empathy here.</div> </div> </div> </div>So when I say you failed to explain your subtext, you instead reply by making assumptions about my character?<br /> <br /> For the record, that old British Sitcom is the perfect precedent to cite:<br /> 1) If it's ok to base a sitcom on WWII then it's probably ok to base most other things on WWII.<br /> 2) I know for a fact that my Grandmother (who grew up Jewish German!) loved Dad's Army to bits. If she loved it, I know it's fair game to use as precedent for acceptable portrayal of Nazi's.<br /> <br /> <br /> So tell me, now that we're apparently bringing our personalities into this. Now that you've disagreed with my grandmother about what's acceptable and by implication questioned a German Jew's empathy towards holocaust victims, why should I consider your views about what's acceptable to be worth listening to at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T06:53:19-08:00","id":17107,"title":"","content":"Sorry, but your grandmother doesn't speak for all of those affected by the holocaust. That's kind of like saying 'well my black friend thinks it's funny, so lighten up'. You haven't addressed what I see as subtext at all, only denied it and insisted that we have to take for granted that this is a sensitive, well-informed example of something that uses the most notorious instance of genocide in modern history as its foundation (and mainly concerns killing monsters like a boss. fuck yeah humanity), rather than question its meaning and implications. If you want a hugbox environment where there are no questions beyond 'do these guys get along with the cambodian version of TFV forum user 77 made for some reason?' then don't expect to be taken seriously as a writer and don't expect this exchange to go anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T07:11:55-08:00","id":17111,"title":"","content":"So my grandmother doesn't, but you do?<br /> <br /> The enormous popularity of Dad's Army in the country which, while less than the holocaust, still faced the enormous horrors of war doesn't speak about acceptable ways to portray WWII in fiction. But you do?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And no, I did not say anyone has to take it for granted that this is &quot;sensitive&quot;. In fact I do not consider myself qualified to comment on that. What I did say is that using previous shows, including one that was enormously popular with the actual victims, as precedent for what is acceptable, this clearly falls within the range of acceptable.<br /> <br /> It's you who wants us to take stuff for granted. I provided evidence for my argument: contemporary views on media containing Nazi's. You have provided no evidence and want us to take it for granted that all portrayals of the holocaust that don't fit into your narrow mould of acceptability are insensitive.<br /> <br /> Next time you want to accuse someone of being insensitive, have some actual evidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-24-2013, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T07:21:52-08:00","id":17112,"title":"","content":"'This is completely fine, because of an ancient sitcom which my jewish grandmother enjoyed,' isn't exactly the same as 'I'm unsure if this treats the holocaust with the tremendous amount of care and sensitivity which pretty much all decent people agree that it deserves', Kings. The comedy nazi thing is a whole other can of worms, which I don't think even applies to this. <br /> <br /> If you don't feel qualified to comment on the sensitivity of this piece of custom content, then do you think you would use it in a game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T07:30:07-08:00","id":17116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=17112#post17112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'This is completely fine, because of an ancient sitcom which my jewish grandmother enjoyed,' isn't exactly the same as 'I'm unsure if this treats the holocaust with the tremendous amount of care and sensitivity which pretty much all decent people agree that it deserves',</div> </div> </div> </div> Please provide evidence that &quot;all decent people&quot; agree with you.<br /> <br /> I have provided evidence that the majority of decent people agree with me, that the Nazi's/WWII can be used in comedies or as the backstory to urban fantasy horror.<br /> <br /> Please do the same, provide evidence of some popular protest, petition or anything that suggests the majority of people agree with you when you say things like this are insensitive.<br /> <br /> Because right now you're asking me to take it for granted that you're right, when I have testimony of actual victims disagreeing with you. In fact, I might go so far as to say that claiming you know better than a Jewish German without any attempt at giving a real reason is insensitive<i>. </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=17112#post17112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't feel qualified to comment on the sensitivity of this piece of custom content, then do you think you would use it in a game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes.<br /> <br /> I might not be able to comment, but I can certainly research the precedents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-24-2013, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T07:40:38-08:00","id":17118,"title":"","content":"No you didn't, Kings. You told me that your jewish grandmother liked a sitcom featuring comedy Nazis and that you agree with her. This level of 'proof' could be easily outweighed by the number of people who deny that the holocaust even took place. If you think that I'm saying that Nazis can never be used (I'm not) and that I need to provide a census to prove that the holocaust isn't something to invoke lightly then I think that's honestly pretty ridiculous, and finding license to do something solely because a hacky book or two, or a decades old sitcom did it, then that seems pretty childish, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T07:56:04-08:00","id":17119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=17118#post17118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No you didn't, Kings. You told me that your jewish grandmother liked a sitcom featuring comedy Nazis and that you agree with her. This level of 'proof' could be easily outweighed by the number of people who deny that the holocaust even took place.</div> </div> </div> </div> I said more than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=17111#post17111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The enormous popularity of Dad's Army in the country which, while less than the holocaust, still faced the enormous horrors of war doesn't speak about acceptable ways to portray WWII in fiction. But you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you had even typed it into wikipedia you would know that it was rated the 4th greatest British sitcom in a public vote and rated the 12th greatest British television program of all time by industry professionals. A little more research would reveal that it is still being shown on air today.<br /> <br /> I would consider that to be evidence that my grandmother's view is the commonly accepted one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=17118#post17118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and finding license to do something solely because a hacky book or two, or a decades old sitcom did it, then that seems pretty childish, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep digging, every post you make shows how ignorant you are.<br /> <br /> (Far from being a &quot;hacky book&quot;, The Laundry Files series, which includes The Atrocity Archive also includes a Hugo Award winner).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=17118#post17118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">holocaust isn't something to invoke lightly then I think that's honestly pretty ridiculous</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm saying that your metric for when it's acceptable to invoke the holocaust is not shared by the people who actually suffered in WWII.<br /> <br /> And I'm saying you have no right to accuse Flyboy of insensitivity when you're clearly so ignorant of what the people who actually suffered think, all the precedent on this issue, and worst of all when you're willing to ignore actual evidence of what the people who actually suffered think after it's pointed out to you without even doing basic fact checking.<br /> <br /> And finally, I'm saying that your willingness to ignore my grandmother's point of view as a single one off example without even looking at the Dad's Army wikipedia page and reading the three paragraphs it would take to realise that it was an extremely common point of view is far more offensive than any amount of hunters formed as a reaction to the Nazis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-24-2013, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T08:06:23-08:00","id":17124,"title":"","content":"You're saying that one person you know doesn't share my views. The rest of what I'm getting from this is that old tvtropes pitfall of knowing what something is and not caring why it is being used, informing your blinkered belief that the (internationally modest) popularity of an old sitcom proves that people today don't really care that much about how the holocaust and its consequences are portrayed. I have every right to 'accuse' (to use your emotive language) Flyboy of insensitivity, because it didn't measure up to my standards, which you're questioning while failing to justify your own as though it should be the default that the holocaust is 'fair game'. I really think you have some growing up to do. Until then, I'll wait to hear from Flyboy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T08:22:25-08:00","id":17127,"title":"","content":"No, I'm saying that at least one country, which suffered enormously during WWII, doesn't share your views. Whether it was successful outside of your home country or not, that is a far stronger set of evidence than what you have provided to support the assertion that your views are commonly held; which is absolutely nothing at all.<br /> <br /> Furthermore claiming that I'm arguing that people today don't care is just wishful thinking on my part. I believe that they do care strongly, but that their standards of what is acceptable are simply different to yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T08:53:07-08:00","id":17137,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how I feel one way or another, but I will say I don't think discussing the statistical popularity of an old sitcom is really the ideal way to defend the idea. I don't think one needs to empirically prove that they consider something tasteless or insensitive, but rather than look at it as an accusation that the creator is the worst sort of person, it's a concern about the idea here. I'm not sure if a re-write could remedy that, or if the OP would even want to do that, but I hardly think it's wrong to suggest that one might want to consider carefully how/if they should use Nazis at all.<br /> <br /> I think inevitably the third reich will fit into the history of a German occult organization, though I'll say for my own opinion that I think it's a bit more ideal to put them in a position which has more indirect inspiration from WW2 than direct.<br /> <br /> So obviously the German Government is very keen on making sure it's never subverted by extremists again, right? In the nWoD, it's very clearly presented that major historic events weren't unduly influenced by supernaturals, though they might've considered it or attempted it, and finally we already have the loyalists of thule. So what if the Bund arose from a later crisis in which supernatural forces attempted to infiltrate the government? The mentality to prevent that kind of subversion of government would certainly fit into their response, and out of necessity to deal with the situation, the Bund could've been formed. In that sense they'd be more like a German equivalent of Task Force Valkyrie who could be used when playing games set in Germany, or maybe they'd pursue a german supernaturals to the United States, or maybe they two might be competing to acquire/protect some artifact, yadda yadda.<br /> <br /> I imagine that might feel less distinctive, but they're just some thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T11:40:59-08:00","id":17195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=17137#post17137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how I feel one way or another, but I will say I don't think discussing the statistical popularity of an old sitcom is really the ideal way to defend the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? This is a genuine question, I'm curious as to your views.<br /> <br /> The way I see it, we try to be tasteful out of respect to the victims. Therefore, by definition, what the victims consider to be tasteful is the canonical definition.<br /> <br /> Examining what media was popular with the actual victims seems like a good way to measure what they considered tasteful.<br /> <br /> <br /> I kind of would say you should have empirical evidence before saying something like this isn't tasteful. I think that if you call everything that uses the Nazi's distasteful, that dilutes the impact. It should be saved for the stuff the actual victims would dislike.<br /> <br /> Of course, everyone's entitled to their own opinion but there's a difference between &quot;I find this distasteful&quot; and &quot;this is distasteful&quot;. Just as an example: Some people find Harry Potter distasetful for it's portrayal of witchcraft but on an emperical level society does not find it distasteful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-24-2013, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T11:52:21-08:00","id":17200,"title":"","content":"The victims don't have a monopoly on being offended is the thing. Above them (and I'd argue that the jewish people as a whole are victims.) we're tasteful because of the moral implications of not being tasteful. Of misrepresenting and making light towards a pretty childish and frivolous application. It's ridiculous and insulting for you wheel out your grandmother and her taste in television to justify using nazis in whatever fatuous way you'd like. 'Canonical definition of an opinion'? Really? I really hope you don't share these beliefs irl, Kings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T11:53:36-08:00","id":17201,"title":"","content":"I guess my concern is that the popularity of a sitcom is information without context. There could've been a million people who liked it or maybe those million people were watching it out of morbid curiousity, or maybe they hated it but kept watching anyway.<br /> <br /> Those are very radical examples, but the point I'm trying to impress is that the statistical popularity of a television show isn't that helpful in portraying why people liked it or didn't like it, or how that has bearings on their ideas of nazi portrayal in media, because it's just telling you that they watched it, not how they feel about it. What works in one medium might not work in another, etcetera. When it comes to dicey issues like how people feel nazis should or shouldn't be portrayed in media, I think it's more nuanced than the popularity of a particular television shows allows, if it's being used as the cornerstone of the argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T12:08:22-08:00","id":17207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=17201#post17201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my concern is that the popularity of a sitcom is information without context. There could've been a million people who liked it or maybe those million people were watching it out of morbid curiosity, or maybe they hated it but kept watching anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a completely fair concern, of course the answer to that is to get more information. (For the record, it was genuinely loved. It not only had high viewing figures but also won 4th place in the public vote for the greatest British sit-com of all time. There was a statue built of one of the characters in the town it was filmed).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=17201#post17201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to dicey issues like how people feel nazis should or shouldn't be portrayed in media, I think it's more nuanced than the popularity of a particular television shows allows, if it's being used as the cornerstone of the argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't deny that it is more nuanced, but when you talk about the issues you have to start somewhere.<br /> <br /> That said, this Compact doesn't require a deep nuanced look at the issues, it is sufficient to find precedent that shows similar portrayals were considered acceptable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-24-2013, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T12:57:54-08:00","id":17251,"title":"","content":"what is happening on this thread?.. 0_0","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T14:44:43-08:00","id":17318,"title":"","content":"I think the Compact is a good idea. The concept is well thought out; it fills a certain niche and you've obviously put a lot of work into Flyboy. I like it.<br /> <br /> I disagree that it is tasteless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T15:26:49-08:00","id":17337,"title":"","content":"My only problem with it is that these dudes are apparently the best hunters in the world.<br /> They seem to be able to identify and know the vulnerability of every supernatural, they can somehow identify changelings (whose Masks are wildly hard to pierce) and deal with their communities (who are wildly insular and can literally drop off the face of the earth in a moments notice) with no problem, despite also being hardcore killers of everything.<br /> Even the international conspiracies don't seem as knowledgeable, and this is just one country that until 1990 was split into two politically opposed ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T21:36:15-08:00","id":17504,"title":"","content":"I'm not gonna lie, I'd be more inclined to listen to Leaper's points if they were less confrontational about it. As of right now, though, all I can see is TheKingsRaven arguing points with logic and examples, and Leaper taking a very narrow minded interpretation of a (frankly very well done) piece of material. So kudos to you, King's Raven.<br /> <br /> Now, as for the controversy surrounding this piece of material.<br /> <br /> I generally look at anything involving Germany that makes even the most tenuous connection to WWII with a very harsh eye. The Holocaust is not something to be taken lightly, or without proper respect. I personally feel this piece is very respectful, and written from a very culturally sensitive point of view. I'm not seeing any ridiculous caricatures, or anything like that. It's very well written, with an interesting theme of twofold fear of the supernatural, and the evil of men. <br /> <br /> Just my two cents on the matter, but there you have it. I support The King's Raven on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","name":"Doctor Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T05:54:56-08:00","id":17665,"title":"","content":"Ah yes. Logic dictates that this sitcom proves that stop being such a baby about the holocaust. *doffs fedora*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T08:23:39-08:00","id":17723,"title":"","content":"I sincerely, truly hope you are being ironic when you &quot;doff your fedora.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","name":"Doctor Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T08:49:04-08:00","id":17738,"title":"","content":"fedora-shaming is extremely triggering for me, buddy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T10:46:02-08:00","id":17803,"title":"","content":"Well... because the Holocaust is a very delicate topic and very close to me (I have family members who are survivors), I also decided to read the compact- and here is my take on it :P<br /> <br /> Most of it isn't bad. While the Holocaust is something one should approach with care, it doesn't mean that using it as a material for a fictional organization is wrong- just that one must make sure to not make any mistakes. Like I said, this writeup is not bad in general. The description doesn't give me any feeling that the Holocaust was the creation of supernatural forces. It does contain a little too much use of terms of a &quot;supernatural lexicon&quot;, which could create an impression that the Holocaust was full of monsters. The reason that the &quot;occult hunting&quot; paragraph feels a little artificial- like, it takes it for obvious that the Nazis had open connections with witches, vampires and other weird things. There is no &quot;revelation&quot; or &quot;discovery&quot; of the supernatural. It is just like &quot;look, the Nazis worked with monsters, so we hunt monsters. Any questions?&quot; (at least, that is my feeling from it).<br /> <br /> What I feel that lacks is.. I don't know, personality? Like, the organization kinda lacks it right now. It is just &quot;We are the good guys, and we try to save our country&quot;. There should be something more... a theme. That's the main thing which I feel that it lacks. A solid theme. If it had a more solid theme, I feel that the writeup could drop few &quot;occult words&quot; and in that way prevent the feeling that there were ALLOT of supernaturals among the Nazis. I mean, if they are simply a &quot;governmental organization which protect the country from the supernatural because they helped the Nazis in WWII&quot;, it sounds a little childish and could potentially make someone to think that the Nazis were backed up by something supernatural. If they had a more specific ideology it could help the reader to feel better that there is a separation between the Nazis and the occult subjects they researched. Still, it could be felt that the writer doesn't try to hint that there was a supernatural &quot;power behind the throne&quot; of the Third Reich, and that humanity is the one which is responsible to the Holocaust (although it could be elaborated a little more, if the writer feels that it would be right)<br /> <br /> TL,DR- The concept is ok, the writer doesn't say that the Nazis were controlled by some supernatural race, it could use having a more solid theme and the writer should tone down the connection between the Nazis and Occult. Those are my two cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T11:17:40-08:00","id":17820,"title":"","content":"Take note Leaper, LostLight and Doc Lazarus just showed how to properly criticize something from an objective viewpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T12:41:06-08:00","id":17858,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how an objective viewpoint exists around such a subject. If I'm offended, I'm offended. I care less about giving you objective criticism and more about voicing that offence. Even less so when your only response to this thread has been a smarmy sentence to the effect of 'your opinion is moot and you should take note from people who are nicer to me'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T13:00:24-08:00","id":17870,"title":"","content":"I'm trying really hard to be civil here, so take anything I say through the lense of &quot;He is trying to be polite.&quot;<br /> <br /> All I'm really getting from you is &quot;I'm offended, and I want to be loud about it.&quot;<br /> <br /> I understand what it is to be offended by something. However, when I am offended by something, I leave it alone. I stay away from it. I don't really understand why you feel the need to harass Flyboy, because of his write up. This is kinda cliche, but I would honestly say, if you don't like it, then don't read it.<br /> <br /> No one is holding you at gunpoint and forcing you to read this write up, or use it in your games. It is purely optional homebrew. <br /> <br /> Honestly, all you are doing is making it hard to discuss Compact: SG-14; The Bund, all for the sake of yelling about how offended you are. <br /> <br /> Again, I'm not trying to be rude, but that's kinda childish, don't you think?<br /> <br /> As such, I've flagged your post, and hopefully, a moderator can sort this out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","name":"Doctor Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T16:07:46-08:00","id":17997,"title":"","content":"So, now that the problem's solved, I've gotten &quot;They're too effective&quot;, &quot;Tone down the occult connection&quot;, and &quot;They're a touch bland&quot;, what else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T17:18:25-08:00","id":18038,"title":"","content":"For effectiveness, I'd say tone down the &quot;all knowing aspect.&quot; Make it so that they have a big knowledge repository, but it is far from complete, and the holes in their information kill people. <br /> <br /> I guess, instead of them already having all the info, give them a focus on finding all of the info. Cells that don't kill at first, but take the time to study, both in a lab, and in the field, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","name":"Doctor Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T07:27:00-08:00","id":18395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1580-compact-sg-14-the-bund?p=17997#post17997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and &quot;They're a touch bland&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To fix this my suggestion would be to put more focus the central theme. This is &quot;Federal Office for the Protection of the Constitution&quot;, you could play that up. The Bund isn't trying to protect Fritz, the average German citizen, from being eaten by a Werewolf. They are trying to prevent Fritz from being indoctrinated by a fascist/evil government or movement. <br /> <br /> Here is some possible ways to reinforce that theme:<br /> <br /> You could make the JAGHUNDs that directly deal with preventing monsters (human or supernatural) from infiltrating or influencing government the top dogs who get the funding, support and win their interdepartmental beurocatic conflicts. Anti-Vampire, anti-cult/neo-nazi/rogue-hunters, and internal affairs are top dog. Witches try to influence governments but not as much as Vampires so they'd be in the middle, while groups like Slashers and Werewolves are the runt of the litter. You might go as far as to say that they only have a silver hound because both vampires and werewolves can turn into wolves.<br /> <br /> You could put more focus on internal conflicts. For example the anti-cult guys might be trying to make it harder for cults to get their message out (Germany does censor swastickers), while another group might be strongly in favour of the free press in the belief that an informed public resists indoctrination. They could be conflicted about using surveillance (&quot;We're not the Stasi!&quot; vs &quot;it saves lives!&quot;). Germany's recent spat with the USA (do they also blame the UK? They probably should do) over the NSA spying might serve as inspiration for another one. Who gives us the right to decide when a democratically elected candidate's politics are unacceptable? Basically, show their determination to not become &quot;The Problem&quot; as an active thing with debates, political fights and conflicts of opinion that PCs can take part in.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T12:00:57-08:00","id":18586,"title":"","content":"I think this is GENIUS!<br /> <br /> First, the organization itself. The way it splits into different specialties, and demonstrates with brutal clarity why that just doesn't work very well in nWoD. The Silver Hounds take out shapeshifters, but what if the shapeshifter is a vampire or a mage with shapeshifting abilities? Black takes out Spirits, but what of Mages with Spirit Arcana or Werewolves? I love how you showed how the crossover potential of nWoD makes this kind of subdivided specialization really more trouble than its worth, yet have a pretty good rationale for why the group doesn't just come together into one uber monster hunting machine.<br /> <br /> Second, the Nazi connection. Nazis are, perhaps, overutilized in fiction as pretty much the ultimate disposable bad guy. As Yahztee of Zero Punctuation said, &quot;Nazis are like Skittles in that you can rid the world of as many as you like and never get a bad taste in your mouth.&quot; Something I loved about the Followers of Thule was how they sort of moved on from that concept, and dealt with the complex feelings of guilt and remorse for what was one of the darkest chapters in human history. I love how this writeup expands that concept, focusing not on &quot;Nazi Germany,&quot; but on &quot;Post-Nazi Germany.&quot; How do people come back from that, and how do they ensure something like it never happens again? And here, I think, is where some people are having a disconnect about respect and taste.<br /> <br /> Sidetrack: See, in the real world, there are all kinds of organizations and laws and such in place in Germany as direct results of that dark time, to ensure those things never happen again. But this write-up is about a group that only exists in the nWoD, and thus only covers the changes from our world to that world. In our world, yes, Hitler and some of his followers were obsessed with the occult, but depending on what you believe about the state of paranormal, they were anything from slightly misguided to completely delusional. They certainly weren't wielding any kind of actual, mystical power of the type available to be found in the nWoD. Now, peering through the nWoD lens, we find that these forays into the occult could actually have yielded results, and like everything else the Nazis did, they left things a gods-awful mess when they fell. Someone has to step in and clean it up. As the same groups we have in the real world go about cleaning up the same messes that exist in the nWoD, this group peculiar to the nWoD appears to clean up the mess peculiar to the nWoD. So, yeah, the write-up focuses on things that are peculiar to the nWoD as well, because that's the point. There's no need to keep belaboring the point that mundane organizations exist to do the same job they do in our mundane world. The write-up never once lays the blame for anything that happened in Nazi Germany squarely at the feet of the supernatural. In fact, most of what ties back to WWII proceeds organically from what we already know about the nWoD. People who die, especially traumatically, can leave ghosts, and the camps killed hundreds of thousands of people very traumatically, so that leaves a lot of ghosts. Spirits are attracted to places that Resonate with their concepts, so spirits of death, fear, despair, torment, anguish, and so on will gather around the camps as well. That's simply a fact of the nWoD. How does that cheapen what happened? In simple literary metaphor, all it does is demonstrate that the horrible things that happened still echo today, that the atrocities can never be undone. All we can do now is live with them. This, I think, is what Flyboy is getting at. He's not saying that Hitler was possessed by a spirit of Anti-Semitism or some bullshit like that, he's just expanding the logic of the nWoD to include the aftermath of World War II and the Holocaust. Moreover, I noticed that he does reference other groups targeted for elimination by the Nazis. Yes, the Jewish people were the first and most prominent victims, but the Nazis sought to &quot;cleanse&quot; the world of so many, many more groups of people. Forgetting just how broad the death toll was cheapens the Holocaust more, in my mind, than noting that it happened and here are the consequences in a fictional world.<br /> <br /> Third, the specialties. I don't personally see them as &quot;know it all awesomes,&quot; but I can see how that interpretation would arise. I think it's mostly from the Status benefits, where higher Status confers more bonuses in regards your specialty monster, and the flavor descriptions of the knowledge that level of Status brings. Tone that down or re-write it, so that even Status 5 characters know just slightly above jack-shit, and that should address the uber-Hunter complaint.<br /> <br /> Fourth, the innovative approach. I love that these guys are invested in not just lumping all monsters together as monsters. It fits with the roots in immediate post-Holocaust Germany, the vow to never again consider anyone &quot;subhuman&quot; just because they are different. I love that they pretty much view every monster on a case-by-case basis, and are perfectly willing to let werewolves and such go about their daily and nightly lives provided they don't hurt anyone. The only places I noticed this break down is as regards vampires and Prometheans. I can understand both to an extent, but would like to raise a few points. Prometheans, given the effects of Disquiet and Wasteland, may very well be viewed as constant threats if people don't figure out that these are things truly beyond their control, and learn a great deal about the core of the Promethean condition, which is difficult-to-impossible due to the nature of the Promethean condition. It's part and parcel of a Promethean's lot in life to be hated and feared everywhere he goes, and this is just another facet of that experience. However, should a Promethean start making inroads with Yellow, and show the group what kind of piteous creatures they really are. . . oh, story potential abounds. With Vampires, I wonder why Red views the only good bloodsucker as a dead bloodsucker. What about the ones just trying to survive from one night to the next? Is Red intent on dismantling the manipulative support structure Kindred invariably build for themselves (which makes sense, given their desire to never see Germany manipulated again), but at the same time, this sort of structure is the only thing that allows Kindred to survive in the mortal world. Is Red fully prepared to sentence every Kindred in Germany to death should they succeed in destroying the power structure that allows Kindred to feed and interact with minimal risk? Do they understand that the nature of the Beast means that dismantling Kindred society will result in things getting way, WAY worse before they get better? Is there any attempt to reach a kind of treaty or truce with the vampires as a whole, or with individual Covenants? Also, I love how Red Hunters are less classic &quot;stake-and-bake&quot; vampire hunters, and more about infiltrating the Kindred and beating them at their own game. I don't think I've ever seen an organization try and take on vampires in their own arena of politics, manipulation, and deceit, and for that alone this idea gets a gold star from me.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think this is a terrific idea, and would totally run a Chronicle based solely on this writeup alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T06:04:04-08:00","id":19120,"title":"","content":"I'll not lie, Rot Jaghund is the way it is because I have an insanely biased opinion against vampires in WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T09:16:07-08:00","id":19214,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if that was the case.<br /> <br /> While I certainly respect everyone's right to their opinion, I might take a more even-handed approach, even to a splat you don't personally like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-